                if matrix[i][j] < matrix[k][j]:
                    matrix[i][j], matrix[k][j] = matrix[k][j], matrix[i][j]

    for i in range(rows - 1):
        for j in range(cols - 1):
            if matrix[i][j] > matrix[i + 1][j + 1]:
                matrix[i][j], matrix[i + 1][j + 1] = matrix[i + 1][j + 1], matrix[i][j]

    return matrix

matrix = [
    [9, 4, 2],
    [7, 5, 3],
    [6, 1, 8]
]

print(sort_matrix(matrix))
```

In the given erroneous code, the sorting logic is incorrect. The code tries to sort the matrix in each row and column, but it does not consider the diagonal sorting. Additionally, the swapping of elements in the diagonal sorting is not done correctly.

